# UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256
#
# Per-file SHA-256 baseline for every upstream byte this package carries.
#
# The complete answer is one line. That is not a thin record: it is the whole
# of the upstream scope, and the sections below are what make it checkable
# rather than merely true. Shewchuk's predicates are distributed as a single C
# file with no header, no build system, no test suite, no test data, no
# vendored dependency, no generated table and no licence file, so a complete
# baseline for this SDK is one digest of one file -- and the coverage check in
# `tools/check-provenance.sh` is what proves nothing else is being carried
# under cover of it.
#
# Verified from the repository root by
#
#     tools/check-provenance.sh
#
# which is also the provenance gate CI runs. The body of this file is plain
# `sha256sum` format, so `sha256sum -c UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256` is a valid
# check on its own; it is the narrower one, because it says nothing about
# whether the path set is complete.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------- pin ---
# project        Shewchuk's Adaptive Precision Floating-Point Arithmetic and
#                Fast Robust Geometric Predicates
# author         Jonathan Richard Shewchuk, School of Computer Science,
#                Carnegie Mellon University
# revision       May 18, 1996, the date in the file header. There is no tag and
#                no commit to record: the file is served from an AFS directory,
#                not from a repository, so the header date is the whole of the
#                revision identity that exists.
# canonical URL  https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/quake/public/code/predicates.c
# project page   http://www.cs.cmu.edu/~quake/robust.html
# report         CMU-CS-96-140
# carried as     src/predicates.c
# licence        Public domain. The grant is the file's own header: "Placed in
#                the public domain by Jonathan Richard Shewchuk". It travels
#                inside the C file, so the one baseline entry covers the
#                licence text as well as the code; there is no separate
#                upstream LICENSE to preserve, and `NOTICE.md` reproduces the
#                grant for a reader who does not open C.
# archive        none. The canonical distribution is a bare HTTP file, not a
#                release archive, so there is no archive digest to record and
#                the digest below is of the served bytes themselves.
#
# These three values are also stated in `UPSTREAM.md`, and the gate fails if the
# two documents stop agreeing:
#
# pin-echo: f8662c3f407d1c1c5dcd4dd49ea8b8ddd801a71827d65734206ddc3741792029 (SHA-256 of the served file; also in UPSTREAM.md)
# pin-echo: 4f199d0294b91b89f2decff591ffa305 (MD5 of the served file; also in UPSTREAM.md)
# pin-echo: May 18, 1996 (the revision identifier; also in UPSTREAM.md)
# pin-echo: https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/quake/public/code/predicates.c (canonical URL; also in UPSTREAM.md)
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------ derivation ---
# Every digest here was taken from a fresh fetch of the canonical URL, on
# 2026-10-04, and not from this working tree:
#
#     curl -sSfL -o predicates.c https://www.cs.cmu.edu/afs/cs/project/quake/public/code/predicates.c
#     sha256sum predicates.c   # f8662c3f407d1c1c5dcd4dd49ea8b8ddd801a71827d65734206ddc3741792029
#     md5sum   predicates.c    # 4f199d0294b91b89f2decff591ffa305
#     wc -c     predicates.c   # 171536
#     wc -l     predicates.c   # 4262
#     cmp predicates.c ../../foundation-libs/predicates/src/predicates.c
#
# The four recorded values agree with the fetched file, and the fetched file is
# byte-identical to the one this package compiles. `UPSTREAM.md` states the
# same digest, size, line count and MD5; the gate re-derives all of them, so a
# table that drifted from the tree fails rather than agreeing with itself.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- counts ---
# count: carried upstream paths in this baseline = 1
# count: upstream algorithm sources = 1
# count: upstream public headers = 0
# count: upstream internal headers = 0
# count: upstream tests and test data = 0
# count: upstream generated-table inputs and generators = 0
# count: upstream build files = 0
# count: upstream data files = 0
# count: vendored third-party files = 0
# count: upstream licence files = 0 (the grant is inside src/predicates.c)
# count: byte-identical to the pin = 1
# count: recorded divergences from the pin = 0
# count: fork-owned paths carried alongside (excluded below) = 40
# area: src = 1
#
# What is absent is as much a part of the record as what is present, because
# each absence is what forced a fork decision:
#
#   * No public header. `include/predicates.h` is fork-authored, transcribed
#     from the prototypes in the comment block at the top of the upstream file
#     (`src/predicates.c:180-429`). Nothing invented, nothing omitted.
#   * No upstream tests and no test data. `test/` is fork work: the behavioural
#     tests, the exact integer/rational oracle they are checked against, and
#     the public-C-surface gate.
#   * No upstream build file and no documented compile line. The three flags
#     `-std=gnu17 -ffp-contract=off -fno-fast-math` are stated by upstream in
#     prose and applied in `build.zig`; both facts are recorded in
#     `UPSTREAM.md`.
#   * No vendored third-party code, no generated table, no data file. Nothing in
#     this repository is a copy of anything except `src/predicates.c`.
#   * No upstream README. See the section below.
#   * No CI configuration upstream. `.github/workflows/verify.yml` is fork work.
#   * No upstream Nix packaging and no upstream lock file. `flake.nix`,
#     `flake.lock`, `devenv.nix`, `devenv.yaml`, `package.nix` and `.envrc` are
#     this fork's, and are declared as such in the fork-owned block below.
#     `flake.lock` resolves to a single `nixpkgs` node at revision
#     `c7def046b9a883d46974757852106483d741586f`, which is the revision
#     `flake.nix` already names in `inputs.nixpkgs.url`: the lock records the
#     resolution of a pin this file's own `flake.nix` states, and invents no
#     input. Its SHA-256 as shipped is
#     `ca3c2564b75f5881752ee00a5218f3263a0d61bb4a1a00bd4fd9b32448214e02`,
#     from `sha256sum flake.lock` on 2026-10-04. That digest is a dated record
#     and not a gate input: `tools/check-provenance.sh` does not compare it, and
#     it is deliberately kept out of the manifest body below, because a
#     fork-owned file listed as a carried upstream path would make this record
#     claim two upstream files where upstream ships exactly one. Recompute it
#     with that one command if the lock is ever re-pinned.
#
# There is no divergence from the pin to record: `src/predicates.c` is carried
# unedited, and the gate checks that on every run.
#
# -------------------------------------------------------------- the README ---
# must-not-exist: README.upstream.md
#
# Every other SDK in this workspace carries upstream's README a second time as
# `README.upstream.md`. This one must not, and the gate fails if the file
# appears: the canonical distribution is a bare C file with no README, so there
# are no upstream bytes to preserve under that name, and `README.md` here is
# fork-authored from its first line to its last. Copying the fork's own README
# under a second name to fill the shape would manufacture a record that does
# not exist. `NOTICE.md` says the same thing in prose.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------- fork-owned files ---
# Every carried path that is not upstream, so that coverage is total in both
# directions: a path that is neither in the manifest nor declared here is a
# gate failure rather than an unnoticed gap. A `fork-owned-prefix:` line covers
# a whole directory of fork work and needs no edit when a file is added inside
# it; a `fork-owned-file:` line is one exact path and does have to exist.
#
# fork-owned-file: .envrc
# fork-owned-file: .gitignore
# fork-owned-file: CHANGELOG.md
# fork-owned-file: FORK-LICENSE.md
# fork-owned-file: FORK-NOTES.md
# fork-owned-file: NOTICE.md
# fork-owned-file: README.md
# fork-owned-file: README.zig.md
# fork-owned-file: UPSTREAM-BASELINE.sha256
# fork-owned-file: UPSTREAM.md
# fork-owned-file: build.zig
# fork-owned-file: build.zig.zon
# fork-owned-file: cross-test.profile.sh
# fork-owned-file: devenv.nix
# fork-owned-file: devenv.yaml
# fork-owned-file: examples/smoke.zig
# fork-owned-file: flake.nix
# fork-owned-file: flake.lock
# fork-owned-file: include/predicates.h
# fork-owned-file: package.nix
# fork-owned-file: src/root.zig
# fork-owned-file: tools/c_surface_gate.c
# fork-owned-file: tools/check-provenance.sh
# fork-owned-prefix: .github/
# fork-owned-prefix: consumer/
# fork-owned-prefix: runtime/
# fork-owned-prefix: test/
#
# ----------------------------------------------------------- manifest ---
f8662c3f407d1c1c5dcd4dd49ea8b8ddd801a71827d65734206ddc3741792029  src/predicates.c
